			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Update editor element submodules to enforce PascalCase naming and clean up lint suppressions\n\nUpdate all tracked editor elements (Air, Common, Grove, Mist, Mountain, Rest, SideCar, Sky) to their latest revisions. The primary focus across the Rust-based submodules (Air, Common, Grove, Mist, Mountain, Rest, SideCar) is the removal of blanket `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` directives. These suppressions were masking violations of the project-wide PascalCase naming convention for functions, variables, and structs. Specific modules including Telemetry, Transport, IPC handlers, and application state layers now enforce strict casing compliance, retaining allowances only for necessary FFI types and C-style constants.\n\nMountain also includes a whitespace normalization pass, stripping redundant leading empty lines following module doc comments across 400+ files to ensure a consistent file header style. Sky is updated via merge to align the frontend UI component layer with the current branch state.\n\nThese changes unify the codebase styling, prevent future naming inconsistencies, and ensure lints are active for all standard identifiers.",
			"SHA": "c8628714895b1154b56ba2af4631df5274b164f3"
		},
